    <div class="lessons">
      <article class="lesson">
        <h3><span class="tag">for</span> Jumlah sudah jelas</h3>
        <p>Dipakai kalau kita tahu berapa kali harus mengulang.</p>
<pre class="code py"><code>for i in range(1, 6):
    print(i)</code></pre>
<pre class="code js"><code>for (let i = 1; i <= 5; i++) {
  console.log(i);
}</code></pre>
      </article>
      <article class="lesson">
        <h3><span class="tag">while</span> Selama benar</h3>
        <p>Dipakai kalau jumlah putaran belum pasti, tetapi ada syarat berhenti.</p>
<pre class="code py"><code>i = 1
while i <= 5:
    print(i)
    i += 1</code></pre>
<pre class="code js"><code>let i = 1;
while (i <= 5) {
  console.log(i);
  i++;
}</code></pre>
      </article>
      <article class="lesson">
        <h3><span class="tag">do while</span> Jalan dulu</h3>
        <p>Blok kode dijalankan sekali dulu, baru kondisinya dicek. Python tidak punya do while, jadi memakai while True dan break.</p>
<pre class="code py"><code>i = 1
while True:
    print(i)
    i += 1
    if not (i <= 5):
        break</code></pre>
<pre class="code js"><code>let i = 1;
do {
  console.log(i);
  i++;
} while (i <= 5);</code></pre>
      </article>
    </div>

